/* The rk4 fit's field error, its drift read through the fixed point.

   A scalar affine field f = c + a x + b u + p w, w the adjustment set's push held over the step,
   on a log of transitions x -> x' at a step h. One RK4 step of it is
   x' = R(z) x + h S(z) (c + b u + p w), z = h a, R(z) = 1 + z + z^2/2 + z^3/6 + z^4/24 and
   S(z) = (R(z) - 1)/z. CHC's rk4 fit is the fixed point theta = G y(theta) of a fit G linear in
   its target, y(theta) = Phi theta + (x' - RK4_theta(x, u))/h, Newton's matrix K = I - G dy/dtheta.
   Its drift regression reads its target at the fitted channel, as the Euler fit's does, and the
   RK4 map moves that target with the channel too; and it moves the channel with the drift's own
   error, so the two errors are correlated where under Euler they are not (Frisch and Waugh 1933).

   Checked here:
   (1) the RK4 step of the affine field, and R = 1 + z S, R' = S + z S';
   (2) at an exact rational point, the fixed point is least squares on the one-step map pushed
       through R^-1: K^-1 G / h = J (X'X)^-1 X', J = d theta / d rho the inverse of the map from
       the field's coefficients to the one-step map's, so in a linear world the rk4 and the Euler
       fits reproduce one one-step map and their one-step predictions agree;
   (3) the drift's block: the drift's rows move with a row's rate by K_rr^-1 W, the channel held,
       and with the channel's error by -K_rr^-1 (Gamma - W Y_c) = -K_rr^-1 S Gamma, Gamma = W u,
       K_rr = I - W Y_r, with K_rr's closed form;
   (4) the field's variance at (x0, u_bar): V_full = V_cond + L^2 V_b + 2 L cross,
       L = u_bar - phi' K_rr^-1 S Gamma, V_cond = phi' K_rr^-1 (D'D)^-1 K_rr^-T phi sigma^2,
       cross = phi' K_rr^-1 W M_b' sigma^2, M_b the channel's row of K^-1 G; the numbers at the
       point, where the cross term takes back part of what L^2 V_b adds;
   (5) the projected action's slope in the state, scalar: da/db = -S(z) Gamma/(R'(z) + g S'(z)),
       g = h b Gamma, from the normal equation's implicit derivative and from K; -Gamma under
       Euler; its pole where R' + g S' = 0, at z = -1.596 for g = 0;
   (6) what each fit reads: on an exact flow, rk4 reads a + a^5 h^4/120 + O(h^5); on a plant stepped
       by the Euler map, a - a^2 h/2 + a^3 h^2/3 + O(h^3), at a = -0.5, b = 1, h = 0.2 the field
       a = -0.5268, b = 1.0536, so a fit of an Euler-map plant scored against a = -0.5 misses by
       an estimand's bias, not by its error.
*/
display2d : false$
ratprint : false$
/* a check that fails stops the batch with "-- an error.", which validation/run_all.sh reads */
vanishes(label, x) := if (if matrixp(x) then every(lambda([e], is(e = 0)), flatten(args(x)))
                          else is(x = 0))
  then print(label, "= 0") else error(label, "is not zero:", x)$
holds(label, claim) := if is(claim) then print(label, "(PASS)") else error(label, "(FAIL)")$
R(z) := 1 + z + z^2/2 + z^3/6 + z^4/24$
S(z) := 1 + z/2 + z^2/6 + z^3/24$
Rp(z) := 1 + z + z^2/2 + z^3/6$
Sp(z) := 1/2 + z/3 + z^2/8$

/* (1) */
fld(xx) := c + a*xx + b*u + p*w$
k1 : fld(x)$ k2 : fld(x + h/2*k1)$ k3 : fld(x + h/2*k2)$ k4 : fld(x + h*k3)$
vanishes("(1) RK4 step - (R x + h S (c + b u + p w))",
         ratsimp(x + h/6*(k1 + 2*k2 + 2*k3 + k4) - (R(a*h)*x + h*S(a*h)*(c + b*u + p*w))))$
vanishes("(1) R - 1 - z S", ratsimp(R(z) - 1 - z*S(z)))$
vanishes("(1) R' - S - z S'", ratsimp(Rp(z) - S(z) - z*Sp(z)))$
vanishes("(1) R' - dR/dz", ratsimp(Rp(z) - diff(R(z), z)))$
vanishes("(1) S' - dS/dz", ratsimp(Sp(z) - diff(S(z), z)))$

/* (2) one-step coefficients rho = (gamma, alpha, beta, pi) on X = [1, x, u, w], theta = (c, a, b, p) */
rho : [h*S(a*h)*c, R(a*h), h*S(a*h)*b, h*S(a*h)*p]$
th : [c, a, b, p]$
J : invert(genmatrix(lambda([i, j], diff(rho[i], th[j])), 4, 4))$
vals : [h = 1, a = -7/10, b = 4/5, c = 1/10, p = 1]$
N : 9$
xs : [3/10, -1/2, 6/5, 0, -9/10, 7/10, 2/5, -1/5, 11/10]$
ws : [1, -3/2, 1/2, 2, -1, 0, -1/2, 3/2, -2]$
/* the logged action leans on the state and on the push */
ns : [1/2, -1/3, 1/4, -3/5, 2/3, -1/7, 1/5, -1/2, 1/3]$
us : makelist(-1/2*xs[i] + 4/5*ws[i] + ns[i], i, 1, N)$
X : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], [1, xs[i], us[i], ws[i]][j]), N, 4)$
D : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], [1, xs[i], ws[i]][j]), N, 3)$
uc : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], us[i]), N, 1)$
XtXi : invert(transpose(X) . X)$
/* a noise orthogonal to X, so least squares returns the map exactly */
rr : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], [2/7, -1/3, 1/5, 0, -2/9, 1/4, -1/6, 3/8, -1/10][i]), N, 1)$
e : rr - X . XtXi . transpose(X) . rr$
xp : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], subst(vals, R(a*h)*xs[i] + h*S(a*h)*(c + b*us[i] + p*ws[i]))), N, 1) + e$
vanishes("(2) least squares on X - rho(theta)",
         ratsimp(transpose(XtXi . transpose(X) . xp) - subst(vals, matrix(rho))))$
G : XtXi . transpose(X)$
Yrow(i) := [1 - S(a*h),
            xs[i]*(1 - Rp(a*h)) - h*Sp(a*h)*(c + b*us[i] + p*ws[i]),
            us[i]*(1 - S(a*h)),
            ws[i]*(1 - S(a*h))]$
Y : subst(vals, genmatrix(lambda([i, j], Yrow(i)[j]), N, 4))$
K : ident(4) - G . Y$
KG : invert(K) . G$
hv : subst(vals, h)$
vanishes("(2) K^-1 G / h - J (X'X)^-1 X'", ratsimp(KG/hv - subst(vals, J) . XtXi . transpose(X)))$
/* the Euler fit of the same log reads rho's map as a rate: its one-step prediction is X rho, as
   the rk4 fit's RK4 step is */
vanishes("(2) the rk4 fit's one-step predictions - the Euler fit's",
         ratsimp(genmatrix(lambda([i, j], subst(vals, R(a*h)*xs[i] + h*S(a*h)*(c + b*us[i] + p*ws[i]))), N, 1)
                 - X . XtXi . transpose(X) . xp))$

/* (3) the drift's block; theta's order (c, a, b, p), the channel b, the drift's rows (c, a, p) */
ri : [1, 2, 4]$
W : invert(transpose(D) . D) . transpose(D)$
Yr : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], Y[i, ri[j]]), N, 3)$
Yc : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], Y[i, 3]), N, 1)$
Krr : ident(3) - W . Yr$
Gam : W . uc$
KGb : row(KG, 3)$
KGr : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], KG[ri[i], j]), 3, N)$
vanishes("(3) the drift's rows - K_rr^-1 W + K_rr^-1 (Gamma - W Y_c) M_b",
         ratsimp(KGr - (invert(Krr) . W - invert(Krr) . (Gam - W . Yc) . KGb)))$
Ss : subst(vals, S(a*h))$ Rps : subst(vals, Rp(a*h))$ Sps : subst(vals, Sp(a*h))$
vanishes("(3) Gamma - W Y_c - S Gamma", ratsimp(Gam - W . Yc - Ss*Gam))$
[cv, bv, pv] : subst(vals, [c, b, p])$
KrrClosed : matrix([Ss, hv*Sps*(cv + bv*Gam[1, 1]), 0],
                   [0, Rps + hv*Sps*bv*Gam[2, 1], 0],
                   [0, hv*Sps*(pv + bv*Gam[3, 1]), Ss])$
vanishes("(3) K_rr - its closed form", ratsimp(Krr - KrrClosed))$

/* (4) the field at (x0, u_bar), its noise's variance over h^2 set to 1 */
ubar : sum(us[i], i, 1, N)/N$
x0 : 2$
hrow : matrix([1, x0, ubar, 0])$
phi0 : matrix([1, x0, 0])$
Vfull : hrow . KG . transpose(KG) . transpose(hrow)$
Vcond : phi0 . invert(Krr) . invert(transpose(D) . D) . transpose(invert(Krr)) . transpose(phi0)$
L : ubar - (phi0 . invert(Krr) . (Ss*Gam))$
Vb : KGb . transpose(KGb)$
cross : phi0 . invert(Krr) . W . transpose(KGb)$
vanishes("(4) V_full - (V_cond + L^2 V_b + 2 L cross)", ratsimp(Vfull - (Vcond + L^2*Vb + 2*L*cross)))$
print("(4) at x0 = 2: V_full", float(Vfull), " V_cond", float(Vcond), " L", float(L),
      " V_b", float(Vb), " cross", float(cross), " L under Euler's form", float(ubar - phi0 . Gam))$
holds("(4) V_full - 5.5823, V_cond - 5.9765, L - 1.4171, cross + 0.8998 within 5e-5",
      every(lambda([pair], is(abs(float(pair[1]) - pair[2]) < 5e-5)),
            [[Vfull, 5.5823], [Vcond, 5.9765], [L, 1.4171], [cross, -0.8998]]))$
holds("(4) L^2 V_b alone would read more than V_full - V_cond", is(float(L^2*Vb) > float(Vfull - Vcond)))$

/* (5) scalar, x' = a x + b u: the drift's normal equation sum x (x' - R(h a) x - h S(h a) b u) = 0 */
Nrm : Sx1 - R(h*a)*Sxx - h*S(h*a)*b*Sxu$
dadb : ratsimp(-diff(Nrm, b)/diff(Nrm, a))$
Gs : Sxu/Sxx$
closed : -S(h*a)*Gs/(Rp(h*a) + h*b*Gs*Sp(h*a))$
vanishes("(5) the implicit derivative - (-S Gamma/(R' + g S'))", ratsimp(dadb - closed))$
/* from K: the reading y = a x + b u + (x' - R x - h S b u)/h, W = sum x . / Sxx */
yread : a*x + b*u + (x1 - R(h*a)*x - h*S(h*a)*b*u)/h$
Wyb : ratcoef(expand(diff(yread, b) - u), u)*Gs$
ya : expand(diff(yread, a))$
Wya : ratcoef(ya, x) + ratcoef(ya, u)*Gs$
vanishes("(5) K's -(1 - W y_a)^-1 W (y_b - u) - the closed form", ratsimp(Wyb/(1 - Wya) - closed))$
/* Euler's step R = 1 + z has S = 1, R' = 1, S' = 0: its own normal equation's derivative */
NrmE : Sx1 - (1 + h*a)*Sxx - h*b*Sxu$
vanishes("(5) Euler's implicit derivative - the closed form at S = 1, R' = 1, S' = 0",
         ratsimp(-diff(NrmE, b)/diff(NrmE, a) - (-1*Gs/(1 + h*b*Gs*0))))$
vanishes("(5) Euler's implicit derivative + Gamma", ratsimp(-diff(NrmE, b)/diff(NrmE, a) + Gs))$
print("(5) rk4 over Euler, S(z)/(R'(z) + g S'(z)), to second order:",
      taylor(S(z)/(Rp(z) + g*Sp(z)), [z, g], 0, 2))$
for zz in [-0.1, -0.5, -1.0] do
  print("(5) z =", zz, ": rk4 over Euler at g = 0", float(S(zz)/Rp(zz)))$
pole : find_root(Rp(z), z, -2, -1)$
print("(5) R'(z) = 0 at z =", pole)$
holds("(5) the pole at -1.5961 within 1e-4", is(abs(pole + 1.5961) < 1e-4))$

/* (6) what each fit reads */
vanishes("(6) R(z + z^5/120) - exp(z) to fifth order: rk4 on an exact flow reads a + a^5 h^4/120",
         taylor(R(z + z^5/120) - exp(z), z, 0, 5))$
vanishes("(6) R(z - z^2/2 + z^3/3) - (1 + z) to third order: rk4 on an Euler map, a - a^2 h/2 + a^3 h^2/3",
         taylor(R(z - z^2/2 + z^3/3) - (1 + z), z, 0, 3))$
zE : find_root(R(z) - 0.9, z, -0.5, 0.0)$
print("(6) Euler map at a = -0.5, b = 1, h = 0.2: rk4 reads a =", zE/0.2, ", b =", 1/S(zE))$
holds("(6) a = -0.5268, b = 1.0536 within 1e-4",
      is(abs(zE/0.2 + 0.5268) < 1e-4) and is(abs(1/S(zE) - 1.0536) < 1e-4))$
